(1) CONTRAST RECOMPUTATION for text-gray-600 / dark:text-gray-400 (the
Budget KPI card's and banner's on-target class) — traced which tints each
surface can actually reach first:
  - dashboard-verdict-bar.html: Health ∈ {green, amber, red, neutral} ->
    band bg ∈ {emerald-50, amber-50, rose-50, gray-50}. The gray-600
    decomposition line (lines 26-33) is wrapped in `{{if $v.HasTarget}}`,
    and HasTarget=false is exactly the Neutral/gray-50 case, so this line
    is only ever reachable on emerald-50/amber-50/rose-50. All three
    apply.
  - kpis.html Budget card: `$budgetOver`/`$budgetHealthy` are mutually
    exclusive and exhaustive whenever `HasCombinedTarget` is true (over:
    `gt Delta 0.0`; healthy: `le Delta 0.0`) and the gray-50 `else` branch
    only fires when `HasCombinedTarget` is false — but
    `BudgetVerdict.{Living,Healthcare}.Configured` (which gates whether a
    per-bucket row renders at all) is only ever true when
    `HasCombinedTarget` is true too (see `BuildBudgetVerdict`: it returns
    early with both buckets unclassified if `!m.HasCombinedTarget`). So
    the per-bucket "on target" text-gray-600 span on the KPI card is only
    ever reachable on bg-rose-50 or bg-emerald-50 — amber-50 is
    architecturally unreachable for this specific card (confirmed by
    reading the template's own conditionals, not just testing).

  Hand-computed (relative-luminance formula), light theme:
    gray-600 (#4b5563) on bg-rose-50    (#fff1f2): 6.879:1  PASS
    gray-600 (#4b5563) on bg-amber-50   (#fffbeb): 7.288:1  PASS (banner only; KPI card can't reach this tint, see above)
    gray-600 (#4b5563) on bg-emerald-50 (#ecfdf5): 7.174:1  PASS
  Dark theme, composited against the real background (bg-*-900/20 over
  body bg-gray-900 #111827; Tailwind v3 rose-900=#881337,
  amber-900=#78350f, emerald-900=#064e3b):
    rose-900/20 on gray-900    -> #29172a -> dark:text-gray-400 (#9ca3af): 6.616:1  PASS
    amber-900/20 on gray-900   -> #261e22 -> 6.406:1  PASS (banner only)
    emerald-900/20 on gray-900 -> #0f232b -> 6.384:1  PASS
  All figures match attempt-2's cited numbers exactly (this attempt did
