not a client-side suppression that leaves an AT-visible remnant, so
ACCESSIBILITY.md point 16 (client-side suppression parity) does not apply
here — there is no live-region/aria-state to desync in the first place.
The literal words "over" / "under" / "on target" are still emitted
alongside (not instead of) the color classes in every reachable state
